  "cleanup_contract": "release gate before backup; kill/wait actual child; join handshake and capture before enumerating all capture-created threads; join each; close all three child streams; retain primary identity, original cause/context and all secondary errors in local cleanup object",
  "limitations": [
    "The actual small subprocess replaces the capture-binary command and DEVNULL stdin with controlled Python command plus PIPE stdin; real stdout/stderr pipe reads, threads and process wait are retained.",
    "The child emits literal listening127.0.0.1:5 as a pipe protocol, not a socket binding or actual HTTP/TLS/browser exchange.",
    "Fake LaunchedBrowser only writes the minimal NetLog for pipe controls. Real browser ownership and live parity are untested.",
    "Held stdout gate occurs after a real nonempty stdout read reaches EOF but before read returns to output.extend; this is a controlled reader completion witness, not a kernel pipe timeout measurement.",
    "The held-reader assertion permits capture to remain pending until the test releases its gate. It proves refusal of partial publication, not bounded capture-owned reader cleanup; the control backup joins are a separate contract.",
    "PermissionError is explicitly injected after the actual read; no native OS read failure claim.",
    "One-second finite snapshots follow actual barriers; five-second gate/handshake/join backups prevent intentional indefinite child/readers; resource guarantees remain contingent on successful OS termination and joins, failures retained.",
    "CS1 daemon stderr accumulation and stderr failure collection remain source findings not independently reproduced by these eight new methods.",
    "NetLog baseline has no target-port input. Exact-port attribution must use the canonical observed listening port in an authorized remedy; no unused port interface was added.",
    "No capture refresh, browser launch, sockets, Python test execution, Cargo or network occurred in author lane.",
    "Independent source review and actual Python3.10 Windows/Linux baseline runs are required before repair."
